{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Sharing the Housework", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Grocery Shopping With a Difference", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 3, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 7, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe ways of solving problems and getting things done in work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "  Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn9le07ob03re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Explaining How Things Were Done", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "  You use <span class=\"italic\">be supposed to</span> and <span class=\"italic\">was going to</span>  to explain how things were done.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use the structure <span class=\"strong\">be supposed to </span>when you want to talk about expectations, obligations or arrangements. You can use this structure using the Past tense to talk about things that you were obligated to do, but didn't or couldn't do. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Weren't you supposed to be going away on a business trip?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The airline was supposed to reschedule for that day but couldn't. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": " I was going to get my jacket cleaned too.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Let's check out, and do the errands we were going to do.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The structure is: <br /><br /> Subject + to be +<span class=\"italic\"> supposed to</span> + verb <br /><br /> <span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">was supposed to be</span> there yesterday, but my flight was canceled. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "**Pronunciation tip**:<br /> When you say <span class=\"italic\">be supposed to</span>, you link the /d/ and /t/ sounds together.  <br /><br /> Like this: Be suppose_to", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use the structure<span class=\"strong\"> was going to </span> when you want to talk about things that you had planned or intended to do.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The structure is:<br /><br />  <span class=\"italic\">was</span>/<span class=\"italic\">were </span>+ <span class=\"italic\">going to</span> + verb <br /><br />  <span class=\"italic\">I<span class=\"strong\"> was going to go </span>to the shoemaker to get it fixed. </span>", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Negative Questions To Encourage Agreement", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " Negative questions have a different meaning than regular questions. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "A negative question can be used to ask for confirmation of something you believe to be true.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Well, isn't that more important than money?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Isn't that always the way things happen? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Don't you agree that puts the customer in a difficult position?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<ul> \t<li> \t<span class=\"italic\">Don't you feel that you're overdoing it?</span> \t\t <ul> \t\t\t<li>(= <span class=\"italic\">I think you feel you are overdoing it.</span>)</li> \t\t</ul> \t</li> </ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "With this type of question, you anticipate that the listener will agree with you and answer 'yes'.  ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to overdo", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to do too much ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Don't you feel that you're overdoing it, though? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le07ob03aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to talk about domestic activities.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "cart", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a small car pushed by hand ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Your cart seems awfully full.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le07ob03aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to take my chances", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to take a risk", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'll take my chances!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le07ob03aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "shoemaker", "type": "name"}, {"content": "this person fixes shoes", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I was going to go to the shoemaker to get it fixed. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le07ob03aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to run errands", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to take a short trip to buy things/do things", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm getting some grocery shopping done and running some errands. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le07ob03aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "organic ", "type": "name"}, {"content": " food that is grown free from pesticides and chemicals ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I wanted to get the organic stuff.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le07ob03aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to reschedule", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to schedule for another time or day ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The airline was supposed to reschedule for that day but couldn't. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le07ob03aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Do a little research on why people think they should eat organic food.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Now write up 10 survey questions to ask people about buying fruit and 